      "extract": "In the last few years the determination of several observables in ﬂavor physics by lattice QCD reached such a precision that both electromagnetic (e.m.) eﬀects and strong isospin breaking (IB) corrections, generated by the light-quark mass diﬀerence ( bmd −bmu), cannot be neglected any more (see e.g. Ref. [1] and references therein). Typical examples are the calculations of the leptonic decay constants fK and fπ",
